# Build artifacts: regenerated by the pipeline, never edited by hand.
#
# Listed by name rather than as `*.jsonl`, because `eval.jsonl` is hand-written and must
# stay tracked — a blanket rule beside it reads as though it were generated too.
#
# `property_type_phrasings.json` was listed here and is not any more. It is a *sample* of
# a model's output, not a build product: re-running `make_phrasings` needs an OpenRouter
# key and a live Supabase connection, and returns different words each time. Nothing can
# reproduce the copy the shipped model was trained on, so it is source.
#
# `train.jsonl` and `validation.jsonl` predate this rule and are held in the index by an
# explicit `git add -f`, so git tracks them regardless of what is written here. Untracking
# them is a separate decision from moving them — and one the move made by accident once
# already, when this rule pruned both from a repo-wide `git add`. See `results/.gitignore`.
train.jsonl
validation.jsonl
